# Angular BAMOE UI - Cursor Rules

## Overview
Angular 19 standalone components application for BAMOE enquiry management with OAuth2/OIDC authentication, GraphQL integration, and Material Design.

## Architecture

### Technology Stack
- **Angular 19+** - Standalone components, signals
- **Material Design** - Angular Material UI components
- **OAuth2/OIDC** - Keycloak authentication via angular-oauth2-oidc
- **GraphQL** - BAMOE Data Index for process visualization
- **REST APIs** - Spring Boot (read) + Quarkus BAMOE (write/process)

### API Strategy
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Angular UI                              │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Read Operations                         │
│  → Spring Boot API (port 8081)         │
│  → GraphQL (port 8080/graphql)         │
│                                         │
│ Write Operations                        │
│  → Quarkus BAMOE API (port 8080)       │
│     - Process start/management          │
│     - Task operations                   │
│     - Signal events                     │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Critical Patterns

### 1. User Extraction from JWT (Backend-Only)

**✅ DO: Let backend extract user from token**

The backend automatically extracts user info from JWT tokens. **Never send user data from UI!**

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Don't send user info
const enquiry = {
  title: this.form.value.title,
  reporter: {  // ❌ Don't send this!
    userId: this.currentUser.userId,
    name: this.currentUser.name,
    email: this.currentUser.email
  }
};

// ✅ CORRECT - Let backend extract from token
const enquiry = {
  title: this.form.value.title,
  // No reporter field - backend adds it from JWT!
};

this.processService.createEnquiry(enquiry).subscribe();
```

**Why?**
- More secure - single source of truth (token)
- Prevents user spoofing
- Simpler UI code
- Backend validates token anyway

### 2. GraphQL for Process Visualization

**✅ DO: Use GraphQL as single source of truth**

```typescript
export class ProcessVisualizationComponent {
  
  loadProcessData(): void {
    // ✅ ALWAYS use GraphQL for process data
    this.graphqlService.getProcessInstanceWithVariables(this.processInstanceId)
      .subscribe({
        next: (data) => {
          this.processInstance = data.processInstance;
          
          // Extract comments from process variables
          const enquiry = data.processInstance.variables?.enquiry;
          this.comments = enquiry?.comments || [];
          
          // Extract nodes for visualization
          this.activeNodes = data.processInstance.nodeInstances
            ?.filter(n => !n.exit)
            .map(n => n.nodeId) || [];
        }
      });
  }
}
```

**❌ DON'T: Mix GraphQL and REST calls**

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Inconsistent data sources
loadProcessData() {
  this.restService.getProcess(id).subscribe(/* ... */);  // REST
}

loadComments() {
  this.graphqlService.getProcess(id).subscribe(/* ... */);  // GraphQL
}
// Results in: Stale data, race conditions, complexity
```

### 3. Comments in Process Variables

**Comments are stored in process variables, not separate API:**

```typescript
// ✅ Get comments from GraphQL process variables
this.graphqlService.getProcessInstanceWithVariables(id)
  .subscribe(data => {
    const enquiry = data.processInstance.variables?.enquiry;
    this.comments = enquiry?.comments || [];
  });

// ✅ Add comment via signal endpoint (returns void)
addComment(text: string): void {
  this.processService.addProcessComment(this.processInstanceId, text)
    .pipe(
      delay(500),  // Wait for backend to update
      switchMap(() => this.loadProcessData())  // Refresh from GraphQL
    )
    .subscribe();
}
```

**Key Points:**
- Comments live in `enquiry.comments[]` in process variables
- Add via signal: `POST /EnquiryProcess/{id}/comment` (body: `"comment text"`)
- Refresh data from GraphQL after adding comments (with delay)

### 4. Angular 19 Standalone Components

**✅ DO: Use standalone components**

```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-feature',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [
    CommonModule,
    MatCardModule,      // Import specific Material modules
    MatButtonModule,
    ReactiveFormsModule
  ],
  template: `...`,
  styles: [`...`]
})
export class FeatureComponent implements OnInit, OnDestroy {
  // Component logic
}
```

**Import only what you need:**
```typescript
// ✅ Specific imports
imports: [MatCardModule, MatButtonModule]

// ❌ Avoid barrel imports when possible
imports: [MaterialModule]  // If it exists
```

### 5. Authentication Pattern

**ConfigService for environment-agnostic auth:**

```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class AuthService {
  constructor(
    private oauthService: OAuthService,
    private configService: ConfigService
  ) {}
  
  configure(): Promise<void> {
    const authConfig: AuthConfig = {
      issuer: this.configService.getOAuthIssuer(),
      clientId: this.configService.getOAuthClientId(),
      redirectUri: window.location.origin,
      scope: 'openid profile email',
      responseType: 'code',
      // ... other config from ConfigService
    };
    
    this.oauthService.configure(authConfig);
    return this.oauthService.loadDiscoveryDocumentAndTryLogin();
  }
  
  getCurrentUser(): User {
    const claims = this.oauthService.getIdentityClaims() as any;
    return {
      userId: claims?.preferred_username,  // ← Primary key
      name: claims?.name,
      email: claims?.email
    };
  }
}
```

**User model aligned with backend:**

```typescript
export interface User {
  userId: string;      // JWT: preferred_username
  name: string;        // JWT: name
  email: string;       // JWT: email
  createdAt?: Date;
  updatedAt?: Date;
  roles?: string[];    // Optional, for UI features
}
```

### 6. HTTP Interceptor for Token

**Automatic token injection:**

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class AuthInterceptor implements HttpInterceptor {
  
  intercept(req: HttpRequest<any>, next: HttpHandler): Observable<HttpEvent<any>> {
    const token = this.oauthService.getAccessToken();
    
    if (token && this.shouldAddToken(req.url)) {
      req = req.clone({
        setHeaders: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }
      });
    }
    
    return next.handle(req);
  }
  
  private shouldAddToken(url: string): boolean {
    // Add token to API calls, not to assets
    return url.includes('/api/') || url.includes(':8080/');
  }
}
```

### 7. Subscription Management

**Always clean up subscriptions:**

```typescript
export class MyComponent implements OnInit, OnDestroy {
  private destroy$ = new Subject<void>();
  
  ngOnInit(): void {
    this.service.getData()
      .pipe(takeUntil(this.destroy$))
      .subscribe(data => {
        // Handle data
      });
  }
  
  ngOnDestroy(): void {
    this.destroy$.next();
    this.destroy$.complete();
  }
}
```

### 8. Process Visualization

**Activity icons based on BPMN node types:**

```typescript
getActivityIcon(nodeType: string): string {
  const iconMap: Record<string, string> = {
    'StartNode': 'play_circle',
    'EndNode': 'stop_circle',
    'HumanTaskNode': 'person',
    'ActionNode': 'settings_applications',  // Service tasks
    'RuleSetNode': 'rule',
    'Join': 'merge',
    'Split': 'call_split',
    'ThrowLink': 'arrow_forward',
    'CatchLink': 'arrow_back'
  };
  
  return iconMap[nodeType] || 'radio_button_checked';
}
```

**Process state colors:**

```typescript
getProcessStateColor(state: number): string {
  switch (state) {
    case 0: return 'grey';      // PENDING
    case 1: return 'primary';   // ACTIVE
    case 2: return 'accent';    // COMPLETED
    case 3: return 'warn';      // ABORTED
    case 4: return 'grey';      // SUSPENDED
    case 5: return 'warn';      // ERROR
    default: return 'grey';
  }
}
```

## Service Patterns

### ProcessService (Quarkus BAMOE)

```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class ProcessService {
  private apiUrl = `${this.configService.getApiUrl('bamoeProcess')}/EnquiryProcess`;
  
  // Create process instance
  createEnquiry(enquiry: Partial<Enquiry>): Observable<any> {
    return this.http.post(`${this.apiUrl}`, { enquiry });
  }
  
  // Signal event (comment)
  addProcessComment(processInstanceId: string, commentText: string): Observable<any> {
    return this.http.post(
      `${this.apiUrl}/${processInstanceId}/comment`,
      JSON.stringify(commentText),  // ← Send as JSON string!
      { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } }
    );
  }
  
  // Abort process
  abortProcess(processInstanceId: string): Observable<any> {
    return this.http.delete(`${this.apiUrl}/${processInstanceId}`);
  }
}
```

### GraphQLService (BAMOE Data Index)

```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class GraphQLService {
  private graphqlUrl = `${this.configService.getApiUrl('bamoeProcess')}/graphql`;
  
  getProcessInstanceWithVariables(id: string): Observable<any> {
    const query = `
      query GetProcessInstance($id: String!) {
        ProcessInstances(where: { id: { equal: $id } }) {
          id
          processId
          processName
          state
          start
          end
          businessKey
          variables
          nodes {
            id
            name
            type
            enter
            exit
          }
        }
      }
    `;
    
    return this.http.post(this.graphqlUrl, {
      query,
      variables: { id }
    }).pipe(
      map((response: any) => ({
        processInstance: response.data?.ProcessInstances?.[0]
      }))
    );
  }
}
```

### EnquiryService (Spring Boot - Read Only)

```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class EnquiryService {
  private apiUrl = `${this.configService.getApiUrl('enquiryService')}/enquiries`;
  
  // Read operations only
  getEnquiries(): Observable<Enquiry[]> {
    return this.http.get<Enquiry[]>(this.apiUrl);
  }
  
  getEnquiry(id: string): Observable<Enquiry> {
    return this.http.get<Enquiry>(`${this.apiUrl}/${id}`);
  }
  
  // ❌ DON'T: Write operations through Spring Boot
  // All writes go through BAMOE process!
}
```

## Material Design Patterns

### Cards with Actions

```typescript
<mat-card>
  <mat-card-header>
    <mat-card-title>{{ title }}</mat-card-title>
    <mat-card-subtitle>{{ subtitle }}</mat-card-subtitle>
  </mat-card-header>
  
  <mat-card-content>
    <!-- Content -->
  </mat-card-content>
  
  <mat-card-actions align="end">
    <button mat-button color="primary">Action</button>
  </mat-card-actions>
</mat-card>
```

### Status Chips

```typescript
<mat-chip-set>
  <mat-chip [class]="'status-' + enquiry.status.toLowerCase()">
    {{ enquiry.status }}
  </mat-chip>
</mat-chip-set>

<!-- CSS -->
.status-open { background-color: #4caf50; color: white; }
.status-in_progress { background-color: #2196f3; color: white; }
.status-resolved { background-color: #ff9800; color: white; }
.status-closed { background-color: #9e9e9e; color: white; }
```

### Compact Lists

```typescript
<mat-list>
  <mat-list-item *ngFor="let item of items" 
                 (click)="onSelect(item)"
                 class="clickable-item">
    <div class="item-row">
      <div class="item-status-bar" [class]="'status-' + item.status"></div>
      <div class="item-content">
        <span class="item-title">{{ item.title }}</span>
        <span class="item-meta">{{ item.createdAt | date }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </mat-list-item>
</mat-list>

<!-- CSS for single-row compact display -->
.item-row {
  display: flex;
  gap: 12px;
  width: 100%;
}

.item-content {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  flex: 1;
}
```

## Configuration Service Pattern

**Central configuration access:**

```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class ConfigService {
  private config = environment;
  
  getApiUrl(service: 'enquiryService' | 'bamoeProcess'): string {
    return this.config.apiUrls[service];
  }
  
  getOAuthIssuer(): string {
    return this.config.auth.issuer;
  }
  
  getOAuthClientId(): string {
    return this.config.auth.clientId;
  }
  
  isFeatureEnabled(feature: string): boolean {
    return this.config.features?.[feature] ?? false;
  }
}
```

**Environment files:**

```typescript
// environment.ts
export const environment = {
  production: false,
  apiUrls: {
    enquiryService: 'http://localhost:8081/api',
    bamoeProcess: 'http://localhost:8080'
  },
  auth: {
    issuer: 'http://localhost:9180/realms/quarkus-realm',
    clientId: 'quarkus-bamoe-frontend'
  }
};
```

## Error Handling

**Consistent error display:**

```typescript
export class MyComponent {
  constructor(private snackBar: MatSnackBar) {}
  
  handleError(error: any, operation: string): void {
    console.error(`${operation} failed:`, error);
    
    const message = error.error?.message || 
                   error.message || 
                   `${operation} failed`;
    
    this.snackBar.open(message, 'Close', {
      duration: 5000,
      panelClass: ['error-snackbar']
    });
  }
}
```

## Routing Patterns

**Route guards:**

```typescript
export const routes: Routes = [
  {
    path: '',
    component: HomeComponent
  },
  {
    path: 'enquiries',
    component: EnquiryListComponent,
    canActivate: [authGuard]  // Protect routes
  },
  {
    path: 'enquiries/:id',
    component: EnquiryDetailComponent,
    canActivate: [authGuard]
  },
  {
    path: 'tasks',
    component: TaskListComponent,
    canActivate: [authGuard]
  }
];
```

**Auth guard:**

```typescript
export const authGuard: CanActivateFn = (route, state) => {
  const authService = inject(AuthService);
  const router = inject(Router);
  
  if (authService.isAuthenticated()) {
    return true;
  }
  
  authService.initLoginFlow();
  return false;
};
```

## Common Anti-Patterns

### ❌ DON'T: Send user info from UI

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
const data = {
  title: 'Issue',
  reporter: this.currentUser  // Backend gets this from token!
};
```

### ❌ DON'T: Mix REST and GraphQL for same data

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Inconsistent sources
loadData() {
  this.rest.getProcess(id);      // Stale
  this.graphql.getProcess(id);   // Fresh
}
```

### ❌ DON'T: Update via Spring Boot

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Spring Boot is read-only!
updateEnquiry(enquiry: Enquiry) {
  return this.http.put(`${springBootUrl}/enquiries/${id}`, enquiry);
}

// ✅ CORRECT - Updates via BAMOE process
updateEnquiry(enquiry: Enquiry) {
  return this.processService.signalEnquiryUpdate(processId, enquiry);
}
```

### ❌ DON'T: Forget to unsubscribe

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Memory leak!
ngOnInit() {
  this.service.getData().subscribe(data => {
    this.data = data;
  });
}

// ✅ CORRECT
private destroy$ = new Subject<void>();

ngOnInit() {
  this.service.getData()
    .pipe(takeUntil(this.destroy$))
    .subscribe(data => this.data = data);
}

ngOnDestroy() {
  this.destroy$.next();
  this.destroy$.complete();
}
```

### ❌ DON'T: Hardcode URLs

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
private apiUrl = 'http://localhost:8080';

// ✅ CORRECT
private apiUrl = this.configService.getApiUrl('bamoeProcess');
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Type Safety
```typescript
// Define interfaces for all data models
export interface Enquiry {
  id?: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  status: EnquiryStatus;
  type: EnquiryType;
  priority: Priority;
  reporter?: User;
  assignee?: User;
  comments?: Comment[];
  createdAt?: Date;
  updatedAt?: Date;
}

export enum EnquiryStatus {
  OPEN = 'OPEN',
  IN_PROGRESS = 'IN_PROGRESS',
  RESOLVED = 'RESOLVED',
  CLOSED = 'CLOSED'
}
```

### 2. Reactive Forms
```typescript
createForm(): FormGroup {
  return this.fb.group({
    title: ['', [Validators.required, Validators.minLength(3)]],
    description: ['', Validators.required],
    type: ['', Validators.required],
    priority: ['MEDIUM', Validators.required]
  });
}
```

### 3. Loading States
```typescript
export class MyComponent {
  loading = false;
  
  loadData(): void {
    this.loading = true;
    
    this.service.getData()
      .pipe(
        finalize(() => this.loading = false),
        takeUntil(this.destroy$)
      )
      .subscribe({
        next: data => this.data = data,
        error: err => this.handleError(err)
      });
  }
}
```

### 4. Conditional Rendering
```typescript
<div *ngIf="loading" class="loading-spinner">
  <mat-spinner></mat-spinner>
</div>

<div *ngIf="!loading && data" class="content">
  <!-- Content -->
</div>

<div *ngIf="!loading && !data" class="no-data">
  <p>No data available</p>
</div>
```

### 5. Date Formatting
```typescript
<!-- Use built-in pipes -->
{{ enquiry.createdAt | date:'short' }}
{{ enquiry.updatedAt | date:'MMM d, y, h:mm a' }}
```

## Testing Patterns

### Component Testing
```typescript
describe('EnquiryListComponent', () => {
  let component: EnquiryListComponent;
  let fixture: ComponentFixture<EnquiryListComponent>;
  let mockEnquiryService: jasmine.SpyObj<EnquiryService>;
  
  beforeEach(async () => {
    mockEnquiryService = jasmine.createSpyObj('EnquiryService', ['getEnquiries']);
    
    await TestBed.configureTestingModule({
      imports: [EnquiryListComponent],
      providers: [
        { provide: EnquiryService, useValue: mockEnquiryService }
      ]
    }).compileComponents();
    
    fixture = TestBed.createComponent(EnquiryListComponent);
    component = fixture.componentInstance;
  });
  
  it('should load enquiries on init', () => {
    const mockEnquiries: Enquiry[] = [/* ... */];
    mockEnquiryService.getEnquiries.and.returnValue(of(mockEnquiries));
    
    component.ngOnInit();
    
    expect(component.enquiries).toEqual(mockEnquiries);
  });
});
```

## Performance Optimization

### 1. OnPush Change Detection
```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-enquiry-list',
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
  // ...
})
```

### 2. TrackBy Functions
```typescript
<mat-list-item *ngFor="let item of items; trackBy: trackById">
  {{ item.name }}
</mat-list-item>

trackById(index: number, item: any): any {
  return item.id;
}
```

### 3. Lazy Loading
```typescript
export const routes: Routes = [
  {
    path: 'admin',
    loadComponent: () => import('./features/admin/admin.component')
      .then(m => m.AdminComponent)
  }
];
```

## Debugging Tips

### 1. GraphQL Queries
Test queries in GraphQL playground: `http://localhost:8080/q/graphql-ui/`

### 2. Network Inspection
Check browser DevTools → Network tab for:
- Token in Authorization header
- Correct API endpoints
- Response payloads

### 3. Console Logging
```typescript
console.log('Process data:', data);
console.log('Current user:', this.authService.getCurrentUser());
console.log('Comments:', this.comments);
```

